 '                ],\n'
 '                "orig": "If a restaurant operator is aware that a dog is '
 'persistently out of control, lunging at people, chasing, biting, defecating, '
 "or violating the house rules but fails to intervene, request the owner's "
 'cooperation, consider asking the owner to leave, or report the case to the '
 'concerned government department or the restaurant management when necessary, '
 'this may be regarded as inadequate management that fails to meet the '
 'requirements on good practice. It may also pose risks regarding the '
 'conditions of the license or permission.",\n'
 '                "text": "If a restaurant operator is aware that a dog is '
